render-review - G5 run001, EFMP-301 Unit 10 Urdu mirror
=========================================================

How inspection ran
------------------
- Worktree commit at build time: 8e974084 (branch 022-author-efmp-301); all 107
  manifest inputs digest-verified against the prepared bundle before review and
  re-verified after HEAD moved to 7ef23ecc (parent committed sibling Unit 8
  review records, which touch no bound input) - see verify-manifest.log. The
  renders therefore reflect the exact bound bytes.
- Site built from the bound tree: npm run build (build.log, exit 0), then served
  with `npm run serve -- --port 4599` (serve.log). Browser: chromium 149.0.7827.0
  driven by Playwright (playwright-core 1.61.1).
- Page inspection: node scripts/render-inspect.mjs EFMP-301 10 --locale ur
  --port 4599 --no-pdf (render-inspect.log in this folder; artifacts
  desktop-*.png and narrow360-*.png plus render-inspect.json under
  renders-agent-g5-efmp301-u10-run001/). It inspected all five Urdu pages
  (index, topic-01, topic-02, unit-assessment, unit-teacher-notes) at
  desktop 1280x900, narrow 360x780 (document overflow, the table element as
  the scroll container, figure spill) and A4 print emulation 794px (clipped
  elements, print figure fit), and ran its SVG viewBox/wordmark geometry pass
  over all eight Urdu SVG variants.
- Figure inspection beyond the shared script: figure-geometry-ur.mjs (this
  folder) loaded each .ur.svg from the served build into a same-origin HTML
  wrapper carrying the site's production Noto Nastaliq Urdu webfont
  (fontLoaded: true), then measured every <text> bbox (getBBox) against the
  viewBox, the mirrored grid dividers and every other text element, and each
  marker path against its marker viewBox. Raw data: renders/figure-geometry-ur.json;
  console record: figure-geometry-run.log. Zoomed defect crops: renders/crop-*.png
  (figure-crops-ur.mjs).

What was found
--------------
- Pages: no horizontal overflow at 360px on any page; every table fits
  (client 328 === scroll 328, scroller NONE); figures fit (client 328,
  scroller none); A4 print shows no clipped elements and all print figures
  fit (w=762 right=778); heading order has no skipped levels; all figure
  imgs served with alt text; dark variants swap under [data-theme]
  (hidden img natural 0x0 is the expected Figure.tsx behaviour).
- Figures (real-font measurement): see findings. Defects that the shared
  script cannot see (it measures fallback-font metrics and checks neither
  marker paths nor the header band): invisible arrowheads in fig-U10-2/3
  (marker path drawn at x=770-780 inside a 0-10 marker viewBox), check-label
  lines clipped past the left viewBox edge (fig-U10-3 -17.5px, fig-U10-2
  -2.5px), degenerate header separator paths in fig-U10-1/4 (M 768 y H768
  V y+4 H12 z draws a wedge, not the EN full-width band), and Nastaliq
  bbox interleaving of adjacent wrapped lines at the EN-derived 16-20px
  line spacing (site's own Urdu standard is line-height 2.2,
  src/css/custom.css:50).

Environment limitations, recorded honestly
------------------------------------------
- No system Arabic/Nastaliq font is installed on this review host
  (fc-list empty for nastaliq/naskh/arabic/urdu), so SVGs rendered as <img>
  (which cannot load external fonts) show fallback glyphs. Figure-label
  Nastaliq legibility could not be visually confirmed by eye: the Read tool
  returned no image content for the figure PNGs on this host. Figure
  conclusions therefore rest on browser-measured geometry with the
  production webfont injected (figure-geometry-ur.json), the same basis as
  the sibling G5 runs. Page-level Urdu renders through the site webfont and
  is captured in the desktop/narrow PNGs.
- The Bash safety classifier flapped (transient automode-unavailable
  errors) during the session; affected commands were retried after doing
  read-only comparison work, per the parent's operational note. No tight
  retry loops; no evidence was fabricated while Bash was unavailable.

